<p>Corpus Christi roof damage insurance claims make up a large share of the property claims filed on the Coastal Bend, and for good reason. Roofs here deal with spring hail, strong straight-line winds, tropical storms, hurricanes, intense sun, and salt air. When a storm damages your roof, the claim often turns on technical questions: what caused the damage, whether it can be repaired, what the city and the state windstorm program require, and how the policy values an older roof. This page covers how roof claims usually work for homes and businesses in Corpus Christi, Nueces County, and nearby communities.</p>

<h2>Common Causes of Roof Damage Claims in Corpus Christi</h2>
<ul>
<li><strong>Hail.</strong> Nueces County hail reports cluster in April and May. Hail can bruise and fracture shingles, knock off granules, dent metal roofing, and puncture low-slope membranes. See <a href="/services/hail-damage-claims/">hail damage claims</a>.</li>
<li><strong>Wind.</strong> Wind lifts and creases shingle tabs, breaks seal strips, peels metal panels at the edges, and tears off ridge caps. The May 8, 2025 storm produced NWS-estimated gusts of 105 to 115 mph in western Nueces County (<a href="https://www.ncdc.noaa.gov/stormevents/eventdetails.jsp?id=1247377" target="_blank" rel="noopener">NCEI event record</a>). See <a href="/services/wind-damage-claims/">wind damage claims</a>.</li>
<li><strong>Hurricanes and tropical storms.</strong> Sustained winds, gusts, and wind-driven rain can damage the whole roof system at once. See <a href="/services/hurricane-damage-claims/">hurricane damage claims</a>.</li>
<li><strong>Fallen trees and debris.</strong> Impact damage to decking, rafters, and trusses.</li>
<li><strong>Fire.</strong> Direct fire, heat, and firefighting damage to the roof assembly.</li>
</ul>

